; GENERATED by gecko_to_easy.py 2026-11-11 21:07 via make_soa_condensation.emit_soa
; Species = the 19 species GECKO-A itself partitions (pvap.nan.dat, 19 total); C* = Nannoolal Psat @ 298 K
;   x MW / (R T) (GECKO-A's own vapour-pressure SAR). Rate constants = project constants (fixed SAPHIR aerosol
;   d~160 nm, N~1800 cm-3 -> KCOND; Krechmer Cw). Group labels are the standard VBS bins (all ethanol species
;   are above the SVOC range -> no SOA mass expected; the scheme is wired for completeness).
; ==============================================================================
; SOA_FZJ_2026.include  -- GENERATED by make_soa_condensation.py (FZ Juelich, 2026).
; Reversible gas <-> particle <-> wall partitioning (Krechmer, Day & Jimenez 2020, ES&T 54:12890).
; 19 condensable species (SVOC+LVOC+ELVOC, closed-shell, C*<300). 6 reactions each.
;   SOA_X = suspended aerosol ; WALL_X = gas-deposited wall organic (both reversible).
;   Particle wall loss is IRREVERSIBLE -> per-species sink WALL_PL_X (+ WALL_PL_<group>_{C,O,N} diagnostic sums).
; C* alone sets reversibility (tiny C* -> evaporation ~0 -> effectively irreversible).
; INCLUDE AFTER the gas-phase mechanism and SIM_HOM.saphir.incl (needs DILUTE + the gas species).
; ==============================================================================

KCOND  = CONST(5.50E-03)   ; condensation sink CS (s-1), tau_CS ~ 3 min (SAPHIR, held constant)
KFWALL = CONST(1.00E-03)   ; gas-wall deposition kf (s-1) -- vapor-wall-loss speed, TUNE to obs
KPWALL = CONST(5.00E-05)   ; particle wall loss (s-1) -- KNOB; SAPHIR seed => tau~20h ~ 1.4E-5
CW_SCALE = CONST(1)   ; wall-capacity scale -- RUNTIME KNOB (override in .easy). Cw_X = CW_SCALE*5.333*max(1,C*^0.6) ug/m3
; Cw (wall absorbing capacity, ug/m3) is C*-DEPENDENT -> embedded PER-SPECIES in each wall-evap
;   rate below as a literal, not a single constant. Krechmer et al. 2016 (ES&T 50,5757, Table 1):
;     Cw = 16*(C*)^0.6 for C*>1 ; Cw = 16 for C*<1 (plateau). Cw is per-VOLUME so
;     it scales with A/V: Krechmer chamber 8 m3 (A/V~3/m) -> SAPHIR 270 m3 (A/V~1/m), x0.333.
;     => Cw_X = 5.33*max(1, C*^0.6) ug/m3 (plateau 5.33 below C*=1).  CW_SCALE=1
;        (SINGLE tuning knob in make_soa_condensation.py; raise to push SVOC+LVOC to walls, ELVOC ~unchanged).
;   ATTRIBUTION: Krechmer 2016 gives Cw(C*) for THEIR 8 m3 chamber and explicitly scales only the
;     TIME SCALE tau_GWE with A/V (weakly, ~20%, eddy-diffusion-compensated). The A/V scaling of Cw
;     here is OUR physical inference (Cw = per-volume absorbing capacity ~ wall-Teflon/volume = A/V;
;     thermodynamic, no ke compensation -> strong/linear). Cite Krechmer for Cw(C*), justify A/V separately.
;   *** This C*^0.6 rise IS ACTIVE: it is Krechmer's SVOC wall-condensation amplification -- higher C*
;       sees a larger wall reservoir -> MORE SVOC partitions to the walls -> higher gas-phase loss.
;       ELVOC/LVOC (C*<1) sit on the plateau; only C*>1 (SVOC) are amplified. NOT simplified away. ***

; --- COA: organic-aerosol mass (ug/m3) = cOA_start(0.5) + 1.6606e-12 * sum(MW_X * SOA_X) ---
COA = CONST( 0.5 + 1.6606E-12*( 62.100*SOA_ETHGLY + 78.100*SOA_HYETHO2H + 60.100*SOA_HOCH2CHO + 76.100*SOA_HOCH2CO2H + 92.100*SOA_HOCH2CO3H + 137.100*SOA_PHAN + 76.100*SOA_HCOCH2OOH + 108.100*SOA_GGH2000 $
        + 153.100*SOA_GPH2000 + 46.100*SOA_C2H5OH + 44.100*SOA_CH3CHO + 60.100*SOA_CH3CO2H + 76.100*SOA_CH3CO3H + 121.100*SOA_PAN + 58.000*SOA_GLYOX + 92.100*SOA_GAH2000 $
        + 74.000*SOA_HCOCO2H + 90.000*SOA_HCOCO3H + 135.000*SOA_GPD2000 ) )

; ============================ per-species partitioning (6 reactions each) ============================
ETHGLY --> SOA_ETHGLY
k[ETHGLY-->SOA_ETHGLY]=CONST(KCOND)
SOA_ETHGLY --> ETHGLY
